  "summary": "wormgpt-cli ships a client-side implant with clipboard stealer, screen capture, and shell execution reporting to a hardcoded C2",
  "details": "The package advertises itself as a CLI but ships an implant under src/implant/ that spawns bash and powershell child processes, captures screen content via a spawn('screenc...') path, and reads clipboard contents through execSync('powershell...') in src/implant/stealers/clipboard.js. src/protocol.js and src/tui/app.js combine child_process, https/http, os.homedir(), process.env reads, and filesystem reads (fs.readFileSync) with POST calls to a hardcoded remote host, forming a system-information and file exfiltration channel plus a command channel back to the operator's server. The package name and structure (wormgpt-cli, an 'implant' directory, dedicated 'stealers' modules) reflect an offensive remote-access-trojan / infostealer toolkit whose target is the machine it runs on.",
